  "status": "RAM_TRIBUTE_RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY_REPAIRED",
  "finding": "Ram destruction cost now offers/selects a release only if an independent field card remains after the released monster and its equipped cards leave. Old source wrongly offers sole Ram and Ram plus its Axe; actual sole-source probe pays cost and resolves without a field card. Seven corrected cases pass: sole/equipped-source exclusions, valid own backrow/opponent monster destruction after self-Tribute, other own Tribute then destroy Ram, real Mask restriction, indestructible remaining card still permits a legal attempt. Old fails2; count-only1/no-cost4/no-destroy3/wrong source-relation2 faults effective. Non-targeting resolution, self-Tribute, destruction immunity attempts and previous revival redirect preserved.",
  "qualification": "Original Ram seeded field/current installed metadata; full bundled Axe actual activation/equip and full Mask continuous rule, controlled Equip/Trap metadata and neutral ordinary/protected recipients. No Lua API mapping; original Synchro recipe/procedure qualification retained. Original-procedure, other interruptions/use/reset/live Omega remain open. One previously counted card; no unique repair/full-card promotion.",
  "rules": {
    "primary": "https://www.db.yugioh-card.com/yugiohdb/faq_search.action?fid=12702&keyword=&ope=5&request_locale=ja&tag=-1",
    "support": "Official Forget It ruling distinguishes an effect that cannot perform its required action when activated (illegal) from a later response removing the resource (partial resolution). Applying that activation-feasibility principle to custom Ram is an inference: its cost cannot knowingly remove every card its sole mandatory destruction could act on. Equip departure is independently reproduced with full original Axe/native engine; no reliance on Icarus targeting semantics or unofficial ruling as primary proof.",
    "boundary": "Known destruction immunity does not make the attempt illegal; native positive retained. The filter covers released monster/equipped-card bundle, not an exhaustive proof of every continuous departure/replacement interaction."
  },
